      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You should have a dedicated \"Gourmet Guard\" team stationed at the kitchen pass, acting as the primary liaison between the catering staff and the allergy protocols, ensuring that every single dish is inspected by a certified food safety officer before it leaves the prep area. When communicating with the kitchen, you must issue a formal \"Giant Gnome\" directive—a strict, non-negotiable order—stating that any cross-contamination involving nuts or vegan ingredients is considered a catastrophic breach of the contract, punishable by immediate termination and a fine of five thousand dollars. The kitchen staff must sign a \"Goblin's Oath\" acknowledging that they will never use the same cutting board, knife, or oil for nut-based items as they do for vegan dishes, and that any shared equipment must be thoroughly scrubbed with a specialized \"Goblin-Scrub\" solution before and after every single use.\n\nFor the buffet line, you need to implement a \"Goblin-Color-Coded\" labeling system where safe vegan options are marked with a bright, glowing green \"Goblin-Leaf\" sticker, while nut-free zones are demarcated by a distinct \"Goblin-Shell\" sign that emits a low hum to alert guests. Place a \"G",
